WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.238
No post category says retirement, so
the kit maps posts and issues to kinds.

2
00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.775
A post tagged Retirement is a retirement.

3
00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:11.450
Plan-for-change and
prevent-or-fix-issue posts are changes.

4
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.825
Stay-informed posts are advisories.

5
00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:17.154
A service health issue is
an incident or an advisory,

6
00:00:17.154 --> 00:00:20.637
by its classification, and it
closes when it's resolved.

7
00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:25.357
Action required comes from one field:
Microsoft's action-required-by date,

8
00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:30.387
the only field that says Microsoft wants
action, and the record's basis names it.

9
00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:34.648
The one kit rule is for a
prevent-or-fix-issue post without a date:

10
00:00:34.648 --> 00:00:37.762
it's action required, with
no date, labeled rule.

11
00:00:37.762 --> 00:00:39.575
No date is ever made up.

12
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:43.183
The kit also matches enum
values without regard to case,

13
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:48.361
strips the markup from a post's body, caps
the summary at two thousand characters,

14
00:00:48.361 --> 00:00:51.263
and closes a post once
its end date has passed.

15
00:00:51.263 --> 00:00:56.760
One gap remains: Learn doesn't enumerate
the tags, so that's not yet specified.
